# ==============================================================================
# Microservice Architecture — Environment Configurations Guide
# ==============================================================================
# Each microservice is an independently deployable component with its own isolated
# configuration and credentials. Do NOT store production secrets in a single root file.
#
# Refer to the individual microservice directories for their respective .env files:
#
# 1. Litestar Root Backend (Python ASGI API, Port 8000)
#    Path: backend/.env
#    Example: backend/.env.example
#    Scope: Neon PostgreSQL, JWT, OAuth, Stripe Billing, SMTP Email, Fernet Encryption
#
# 2. Next.js SaaS Web Dashboard (Frontend, Port 3000)
#    Path: website/.env.local
#    Example: website/.env.example
#    Scope: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
#
# 3. Agent Bridge Bot (Python Discord Bot & FastAPI Config API, Port 8003)
#    Path: agent-bridge/.env
#    Example: agent-bridge/.env.example
#    Scope: Discord Token, Gemini AI Models, Taiga PM, Redis, Mongo, Kafka Bridge,
#           Root Backend Identity Client & Strict Zero-Token Guard
#
# 4. Scrum Master AI (Fastify Node.js Discord Voice Bot, Port 3001)
#    Path: scrum-master-ai/.env
#    Example: scrum-master-ai/.env.example
#    Scope: Discord Voice Token, Gemini Live API, MongoDB Meetings, Kafka Producer
#
# 5. Docker Infrastructure (Kafka, MongoDB, Redis)
#    Path: docker/docker-compose.yml
#    Scope: Standalone container orchestration mapped directly to per-service env files.
# ==============================================================================
